      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U5 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "These Ethernet differential transmit pins should be routed to the RJ45 jack or left unconnected/terminated, not shorted to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "Shorts the SKW92A Ethernet PHY outputs to ground, potentially damaging the module and disabling LAN port 3.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 value is 0.1uF/16V.",
      "expected": "The specification requires C1 to be 1uF/25V (C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"}
      ],
      "impact": "Reduced decoupling capacitance and lower voltage rating on the EPD power rail, potentially causing display instability.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1uF capacitor with pin 1 on net unconnected-(C11-Pad1) and pin 2 on GND; its footprint is Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder while its library part is Device:C.",
      "expected": "Both terminals of a capacitor should be connected to the intended circuit, and a capacitor should use a capacitor footprint.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "C11 is electrically inert; if intended as decoupling, the missing connection removes its effect. The wrong footprint may also cause assembly issues.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain several deviations: most critically, U5 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+/-) are shorted to GND, which would damage or disable the Ethernet PHY. Additionally, C1 has the wrong value/rating versus the specification, and C11 is left with a floating terminal and an incompatible footprint."
}

